4. Attribution for unchanged and modified reuse

For the standalone execution and reproduction allowed by Section 2, preserve
the existing project notices. Published reproduction or evaluation results
must credit Jeongwoo Kim and link to the source repository in the report,
paper, or accompanying documentation; no separate permission is required.

For reuse in another work or project under Section 3, unchanged or modified,
retain the existing notices and include Jeongwoo Kim in a clearly visible
section titled "Contributions" (or its local-language equivalent, such as
"기여") in the using project's README or equivalent documentation. Identify
the contribution accurately as the original reused sVLM-Debiasing code and
include the project URL. The following wording satisfies this requirement:

Jeongwoo Kim - original author of the sVLM-Debiasing project code reused here.
Source: https://github.com/jeongwoo-gobroad/sVLM-Debiasing

For a private or internal project, maintain the credit in its internal project
documentation; this clause does not require public release. When publishing a
paper or report based on the authorized code use, also include equivalent
credit in its contributions, acknowledgments, or code-availability statement.
When distributing a modified version, clearly identify that it was modified
and distinguish the modifier's changes from the Author's original work.

This credit records code provenance. It does not imply that the Author worked
on, reviewed, endorsed, or coauthored the downstream project or publication.
It does not require adding a paper coauthor or altering GitHub commit authors
or the automatically generated contributors list. No trademark or endorsement
rights are granted. Only an express separate agreement with the Author can
change these attribution requirements for the agreed use.

